; Cram integration tests for the mathc CLI.
;
; Each *.t file is both the test and the fixture: cram compares
; captured stdout/stderr against the expected snapshot below each
; `$ command`. `dune runtest` aggregates pass/fail; this is the
; gate that the previous `tests/fixtures/cli-*.sh` family provided.
;
; Binary exposure: (deps %{bin:mathc}) requires (public_name mathc)
; in bin/dune. dune installs mathc to
; _build/install/default/bin/mathc and adds it to the PATH of
; every cram test that declares the dep.
;
; Path portability: each test does `cd "$DUNE_SOURCEROOT"` first
; so mathc sees project-relative paths and echoes them back,
; keeping the .t files portable across machines without
; scrubbing. $DUNE_SOURCEROOT is exported by dune.
;
; Non-deterministic fields (e.g. JSON `now` timestamps): pipe
; through `jq -c 'del(.now)'` to scrub before comparison. Dune
; cram does not implement regex/glob output matchers; see
; OCAML_BEST_PRACTICES §11.20 caveat 2.

(cram
 (applies_to whole_subtree)
 (deps %{bin:mathc}))
